course: dictionary
lesson: 10953
title: Many meanings of walk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings. Walk is a good example: it can be a verb, something you do, or a noun, a thing you go on. «Walk, never run, in the kitchen» uses walk as a verb: move on foot, more slowly than running.
explain: A walk can also be a trip on foot, often for fun or exercise, as in «go for a walk». Read the words around walk to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: Some meanings are casual or rough. «It's a walk in the park» means very easy, and «walk it» means win easily. «Take a walk» means go away. These meanings are not about feet at all, so the context is your clue.
explain: Use the swap test. «So walk wide around swings» means move on foot and keep a good distance from them. That makes sense, so walk is a verb here, meaning to move on foot.
fact: Walk can be a verb (walk, walks, walked, walking) or a noun (a walk, walks).
fact: As a verb, walk means to move by putting one foot in front of the other, more slowly than running.
fact: As a noun, a walk is a trip on foot, often for fun or exercise.
fact: «To walk a dog» means to take it out for a walk.
fact: «A walk in the park» means very easy, and «walk it» means win easily.
exercise: «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» What does walk mean here? | Leave in protest | *Move on foot, more slowly than running | Win easily | A trip on foot for fun
exercise: Ravi and his gran go for a walk in the park after tea. What is a walk in this sentence? | *A trip on foot, often for fun | A kind of job | To leave in protest | To steal something
exercise: Mum says «Take a walk!» in a cross voice because she wants me to go away. What does «take a walk» mean? | Walk home from school | Go for a walk with her | Walk faster | *Go away
test: In «walk to school», what kind of word is walk? | *Verb | Pronoun | Noun | Adjective
test: «We will walk the dog after tea.» What does «walk the dog» mean? | Teach the dog to talk | Give the dog a bath | Run the dog to the park quickly | *Take the dog out for a walk
exam: «The hike was a walk in the park.» What does this mean? | Dangerous and steep | Wet and muddy | *Very easy | Very long and tiring
